From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: nvmem: add MediaTek device information

The calibration data of the MT6897 is not read from the efuse block. The
boot firmware passes a copy of the fuses in the atag,devinfo property of
/chosen, and the offsets used for the calibration data are offsets into
that copy. They don't match the efuse block: the vendor kernel reads
some GPU fuses from it at offsets beyond the end of the copy.
---
 .../nvmem/mediatek,mt6897-devinfo.yaml        | 47 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 47 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/nvmem/mediatek,mt6897-devinfo.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/nvmem/mediatek,mt6897-devinfo.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e694096
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/nvmem/mediatek,mt6897-devinfo.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/nvmem/mediatek,mt6897-devinfo.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: MediaTek device information from the boot firmware
+
+description:
+  The fuses that hold the calibration data of the MT6897 are not read through
+  the efuse block. The boot firmware copies them to the atag,devinfo property
+  of /chosen, as a count of 32-bit words followed by the words. The offsets of
+  the NVMEM cells are offsets into those words.
+
+maintainers:
+  - buntOS contributors <buntos@localhost>
+
+allOf:
+  - $ref: nvmem.yaml#
+
+properties:
+  $nodename:
+    const: efuse
+
+  compatible:
+    const: mediatek,mt6897-devinfo
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+
+unevaluatedProperties: false
+
+examples:
+  - |
+    efuse {
+        compatible = "mediatek,mt6897-devinfo";
+
+        nvmem-layout {
+            compatible = "fixed-layout";
+            #address-cells = <1>;
+            #size-cells = <1>;
+
+            calib@310 {
+                reg = <0x310 0x38>;
+            };
+        };
+    };
